        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0233" n="209" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg209"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Judd to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 61.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Berlin,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 7, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi>Your despatch, No. 68, dated March 14, is
                    received.</p>
                <p>I enclose herewith copies of letters between Mr. Sundell, consul at Stettin, and
                    myself in relation to the blockade of the port of Swinemünde.</p>
                <p>I hope that the advice I gave Mr. Sundell will meet your approval</p>
                <p>Respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>N. B. JUDD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
